<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<p>
    <p>Note: you can copy these symbols to express kets: |0⟩. You can express square roots (<m>\sqrt{2}</m>)
        as <c>sqrt(2)</c>. </p>
    <p>Note: if you are familiar with LaTeX, you can use dollar signs ($) to write math using LaTeX.
        You can use <c>\rangle</c> for the angled bracket at the end of kets (⟩) and <c>\sqrt{...}</c> for square
        roots. <term>Using LaTeX is absolutely not a requirement!</term></p>
</p>
